    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Write $\\rho_p=\\operatorname{diag}(1-p,p)$ for a diagonal qubit state. Set $a=\\pi/12$ and\n$$\\mathcal S_a=\\{\\rho_{\\sin^2\\theta}:a\\le\\theta\\le\\pi/4\\},\\qquad T_a(\\rho_{\\sin^2\\theta})=\\rho_{\\sin^2(\\theta-a)}.$$\nOn this family, $T_a$ preserves root fidelity and contracts trace distance for every pair, but it sends the finite input relative entropy $D(\\rho_{\\sin^2(\\pi/4)}\\|\\rho_{\\sin^2 a})$ to $D(\\rho_{\\sin^2(\\pi/4-a)}\\|\\rho_0)=+\\infty$. The map is nonlinear and is not the restriction of a quantum channel. Thus metric inequalities on a family under an arbitrary map do not by themselves prove quantum-relative-entropy data processing for channels.\n\nAs a separate support check, $|0\\rangle\\langle0|$ and $|+\\rangle\\langle+|$ have root fidelity and trace distance both $1/\\sqrt2$, while $D(|0\\rangle\\langle0|\\| |+\\rangle\\langle+|)=+\\infty$."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
    "id": "def-it-finite-quantum-information-measures",
    "target": "items/def-it-finite-quantum-information-measures.md",
    "current_sha256": "16074942fe6a56d2ecce8e02f6b77a2855123fefb32915ba5f8eebe7fca12b13",
    "proposal": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum/proposal/items/def-it-finite-quantum-information-measures.md",
    "proposal_sha256": "fbffeff2c8fdb07c5bca84fab002f29f07a3f3f4ca27c79436446956f065dfdf",
    "deps": [
      "def-it-von-neumann-entropy",
      "lem-it-partial-traces-of-a-state-are-states",
      "def-qc-density-operator",
      "def-non-negative-and-positive-operator",
      "def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces",
      "def-qc-partial-trace",
      "def-qc-first-factor-partial-trace",
      "def-qc-tensor-register-and-permutation",
      "thm-qc-wire-permutation-is-unitary",
      "thm-trace-of-ab-equals-trace-of-ba",
      "thm-adjoint-exists-and-is-unique-in-finite-dimension"
    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Definition",
      "text": "For a finite bipartite state $\\rho_{AB}$ on the ordered product $H_A\\otimes H_B$, write $\\rho_A=\\operatorname{Tr}_B\\rho_{AB}$ and $\\rho_B=\\operatorname{Tr}_A\\rho_{AB}$, using the partial traces in [[def-qc-partial-trace]] and [[def-qc-first-factor-partial-trace]]. They are states by [[lem-it-partial-traces-of-a-state-are-states]]. Define\n\n$$S(A)_\\rho:=S(\\rho_A),\\qquad S(A\\mid B)_\\rho:=S(\\rho_{AB})-S(\\rho_B),\\qquad I(A:B)_\\rho:=S(\\rho_A)+S(\\rho_B)-S(\\rho_{AB}).$$\n\nFor a finite tripartite state $\\rho_{ABC}$ on the ordered product $H_A\\otimes H_B\\otimes H_C$, set $\\rho_{AB}:=\\operatorname{Tr}_{H_C}\\rho_{ABC}$ after identifying the factors as $(H_A\\otimes H_B)\\otimes H_C$, and $\\rho_{BC}:=\\operatorname{Tr}_{H_A}\\rho_{ABC}$ after identifying them as $H_A\\otimes(H_B\\otimes H_C)$. Let $P:H_A\\otimes H_B\\otimes H_C\\to H_A\\otimes H_C\\otimes H_B$ be the wire permutation taking factor order $A,B,C$ to $A,C,B$ ([[def-qc-tensor-register-and-permutation]], [[thm-qc-wire-permutation-is-unitary]]) whose unique adjoint $P^*$ exists by [[thm-adjoint-exists-and-is-unique-in-finite-dimension]], and set $\\rho_{AC}:=\\operatorname{Tr}_{H_B}(P\\rho_{ABC}P^*)$, tracing out the last factor. Because $P$ is unitary, $P\\rho_{ABC}P^*$ is a state: unitary conjugation preserves non-negativity by the adjoint identity ([[def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces]], [[def-non-negative-and-positive-operator]]) and preserves trace by cyclicity ([[thm-trace-of-ab-equals-trace-of-ba]]). Finally set $\\rho_C:=\\operatorname{Tr}_{H_B}\\rho_{BC}$. All these marginals are density operators by applying [[lem-it-partial-traces-of-a-state-are-states]] after grouping factors. Define\n\n$$I(A:B\\mid C)_\\rho:=S(\\rho_{AC})+S(\\rho_{BC})-S(\\rho_C)-S(\\rho_{ABC}).$$\n\nThese are finite-dimensional definitions only; no non-negativity of conditional entropy or conditional mutual information is part of the notation."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
