    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $H$ be a nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product space and let $(E_y)_{y\\in\\Omega}$ be a finite POVM on $H$, where $\\Omega=\\{y_0,\\ldots,y_{m-1}\\}$ is a fixed enumeration of its nonempty outcome set. Let $K=\\mathbb C^m$ with standard orthonormal basis $(f_0,\\ldots,f_{m-1})$, and set $\\Pi_jz:=\\langle z,f_j\\rangle f_j$, the rank-one projection onto $f_j$ under the root linear-first convention. The map $\\mathcal M_E(X):=\\sum_{j<m}\\operatorname{tr}(XE_{y_j})\\Pi_j$ is a quantum channel from $H$ to $K$. For the indexed register $\\mathbb C^\\Omega$ with orthonormal basis $|y\\rangle$, the unitary identification $Jf_j=|y_j\\rangle$ gives the equivalent channel $X\\mapsto\\sum_{y\\in\\Omega}\\operatorname{tr}(E_yX)|y\\rangle\\langle y|=J\\mathcal M_E(X)J^*$. Thus either finite outcome-register convention is covered."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
