      "thm-kernel-and-fibres-of-complex-exponential",
      "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity"
    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $D\\ge2$, $1\\le K\\le D$, and $\\omega_{AE}\\succeq0$ with $\\dim A=D$, $\\operatorname{tr}\\omega\\le1$, and $r=\\operatorname{rank}\\omega_E$. For every $\\delta>0$ there is an explicitly specified finite probability ensemble of isometries $W:\\mathbb C^K\\to\\mathbb C^D$ such that, for\n$$\\omega^W_{RE}=\\frac DK(W^T\\otimes I_E)\\omega_{AE}(\\overline W\\otimes I_E),$$\none has\n$$\\mathbb E\\left\\|\\omega^W_{RE}-\\frac{I_R}{K}\\otimes\\omega_E\\right\\|_1\\le\\sqrt{2Kr\\operatorname{tr}(\\omega_{AE}^2)}+\\delta.$$\nAt the same time the ensemble can be required to satisfy, for every Hermitian $Z_{AE}$,\n$$\\mathbb E\\left\\|\\frac DK(W^T\\otimes I)Z(\\overline W\\otimes I)\\right\\|_1\\le(1+\\delta)\\|Z\\|_1.$$\nNo Haar existence or Gaussian-law supplier, and no choice axiom, is used."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch24-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
    "id": "lem-it-inverse-compression-resolvent",
    "target": "items/lem-it-inverse-compression-resolvent.md",
    "current_sha256": "732dde48876ec413c76dc3bba7dd00e87a3f1e3ad00ff69ce3006f4f4ccfb940",
    "proposal": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum/proposal/items/lem-it-inverse-compression-resolvent.md",
    "proposal_sha256": "e54d702565b63b91275c6fd98bd89e6504d9dffeb0671c3bb22bf502fb8a530c",
    "deps": [
      "def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space",
      "def-adjoint-of-a-linear-map-between-inner-product-spaces",
      "def-non-negative-and-positive-operator",
      "thm-non-negative-operator-characterisations",
      "thm-adjoint-exists-and-is-unique-in-finite-dimension"
    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $H,K$ be finite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces, let $T:K\\to K$ be positive definite, and let $V:H\\to K$ satisfy $V^*V=I_H$. For every $s\\ge0$,\n\n$$V^*(T+sI_K)^{-1}V\\succeq(V^*TV+sI_H)^{-1},$$\n\nwhere $A\\succeq B$ means that $A-B$ is non-negative. If $H=\\{0\\}$, both sides are the unique endomorphism of $H$."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
