      "thm-ftc-second-part",
      "thm-non-negative-operator-characterisations"
    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $H,K$ be finite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces, let $T:K\\to K$ be positive definite, and let $V:H\\to K$ satisfy $V^*V=I_H$. Then, in the non-negative operator order,\n\n$$-\\ln(V^*TV)\\preceq V^*(-\\ln T)V,$$\n\nwhere $R\\preceq S$ means $S-R$ is non-negative and logarithms of positive-definite operators are defined by finite spectral calculus."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
