    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $H_A,H_B,H_C$ be nonzero finite-dimensional complex inner-product spaces and let $\\rho_{ABC}$ be a density operator on their ordered tensor product. Write $\\rho_{AB},\\rho_{BC},\\rho_B$ for its marginals using the partial traces in [[def-qc-partial-trace]]. Then\n$$S(\\rho_{AB})+S(\\rho_{BC})\\ge S(\\rho_B)+S(\\rho_{ABC}),$$\nwhere $S(\\rho)=-\\operatorname{tr}(\\rho\\ln\\rho)$ with $0\\ln0:=0$ as in [[def-it-von-neumann-entropy]]."
