    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "On the qubit space with computational basis $|0\\rangle,|1\\rangle$, define the dephasing channel\n$$\\Delta(X)=|0\\rangle\\langle0|X|0\\rangle\\langle0|+|1\\rangle\\langle1|X|1\\rangle\\langle1|.$$\nFor $|+\\rangle=(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt2$ and $\\rho=|+\\rangle\\langle+|$, $\\sigma=\\operatorname{diag}(3/4,1/4)$, one has\n$$D(\\rho\\|\\sigma)=\\tfrac12\\ln(16/3)>\\tfrac12\\ln(4/3)=D(\\Delta(\\rho)\\|\\Delta(\\sigma)).$$\nFor the orthogonal pure states $|+\\rangle,| -\\rangle=(|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)/\\sqrt2$, the input relative entropy is $+\\infty$, whereas both dephased states equal $I/2$ and their relative entropy is $0$."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch21-owner-addendum"
  },
  {
