    ],
    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $\\mathcal N_i:A_i\\to B_i$ for $i=1,2$ be finite-dimensional degradable channels with complements $\\mathcal N_i^c=\\mathcal D_i\\circ\\mathcal N_i$. Then $\\rho\\mapsto I_c(\\rho,\\mathcal N_i)$ is concave and nonnegative. For every joint input state $\\rho_{A_1A_2}$,\n\n$$I_c(\\rho_{A_1A_2},\\mathcal N_1\\otimes\\mathcal N_2)\\le I_c(\\rho_{A_1},\\mathcal N_1)+I_c(\\rho_{A_2},\\mathcal N_2).$$\n\nConsequently the supremum coherent information of $\\mathcal N_1\\otimes\\mathcal N_2$ is the sum of the two single-channel suprema."
    },
    "source_packet": "research/non-ml-math-remaining-81-2026-10-18-owner-step2-qre-resolution/batch24-owner-addendum"
  },
