    "public_export": {
      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Fix any finite input ensemble $(p_x,\\rho_x)$ for a finite-dimensional channel $\\mathcal N$ and a complement $\\mathcal N^c$. Let $\\chi_B,\\chi_E$ be the Holevo informations of their output ensembles. Every $0<R<\\chi_B-\\chi_E$ admits uniform $M_n$-message codes with mixed input states, Bob POVMs, $n^{-1}\\ln M_n\\to R$, average error tending to zero, and unnormalized complementary-output Holevo leakage tending to zero. The construction has exponentially decaying average error and average trace distance to a fixed complementary product target; dimension-dependent entropy control converts the latter to strong Holevo secrecy."
    },
