      "section": "Statement",
      "text": "Let $\\tau=JJ^*/D$ be the flat state of a nonzero $D$-dimensional input subspace of a finite-dimensional channel $\\mathcal N$. With prior shared maximally entangled states on that subspace, every $0\\le R<S(\\tau)+I_c(\\tau,\\mathcal N)$ is achievable for classical messages with average error tending to zero. The code consists of finite Weyl operations followed by a collective output/reference POVM; it has rate tending to $R$."
